[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137240,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intratarsal cysts are benign keratin-containing cysts derived from Meibomian gland ducts.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137241,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137242,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F36.4 Cysts of eyelid</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137243,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> intratarsal keratinous cyst; tarsal epithelial cyst; Meibomian gland ductal cyst.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> intratarsal inclusion cyst; keratocyst; keratic cyst.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137244,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137245,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intratarsal keratinous cysts arise within the tarsus of the eyelids, with a predilection for the upper eyelids.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137246,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intratarsal keratinous cysts present as painless, well-defined firm nodules fixed to the tarsus, with no signs of inflammation or attachment to the skin. Eyelid eversion reveals a cream-coloured, yellowish, or sometimes blue-grey well-defined intratarsal nodule without associated inflammation {32826823;19875094;29287708;32367161}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137247,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sporadic cysts are most common and are usually isolated lesions in the upper eyelids of older individuals (aged in their fifties to seventies). Multiple cysts, cysts in the lower eyelids, or cysts in a young patient can be associated with naevoid basal cell carcinoma syndrome (Gorlin syndrome) {29287708}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137248,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology of intratarsal keratinous cysts is not clear. Some cysts are associated with Meibomian gland blockage, trauma, and naevoid basal cell carcinoma syndrome {29287708;32367161;24403898}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137249,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Blockage of a Meibomian gland duct with secondary dilation is one of the postulated mechanisms {32367161;24403898}. The rare association with naevoid basal cell carcinoma syndrome raises speculation that some cysts may arise from alterations in the sonic hedgehog signalling pathway genes {29287708}, analogous to odontogenic keratocysts {19362041}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137250,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesions are circumscribed and grey to yellow or bluish with a milky or keratinous luminal material.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137251,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cysts have a characteristic stratified squamous epithelial lining that is 4&ndash;6&nbsp;cells thick, with the basal layer consisting of hyperchromatic cells with stringy eosinophilic cuticle in the lumen. The lining cells lack keratohyaline granules and display a corrugated, brightly eosinophilic cuticle similar to that in odontogenic keratocyst and steatocystoma.</p>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry is not required for diagnosis. The lining cells and keratin are strongly positive for CK17 while the luminal portion of the lining and the contents may be positive for CEA and EMA {30439722;19875094}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137252,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137253,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137254,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> intratarsal location with a characteristic lining featuring corrugated eosinophilic cuticle without keratohyaline granules.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137255,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 137256,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 40,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Treatment consists of complete excision of the cyst lining; partial excision may lead to recurrence.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T14:58:41"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]